{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The region of Argob.</b> The words of the translator [Onkelos] in Aramaic are well known. And some say that he was a person's name — this region was in his inherited portion from his father's inheritance. And some say that the alef is added and it is from the root ורגבים ידובקו (and clods stick together), by way of analogy [i.e., from the same root]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:04.923392234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}